WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.870
Game of Thrones fans know they need to be
on high alert while watching.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:07.970
Whether you're a diehard fan or casual viewer,
it's always fun to hunt for clues with big

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:11.820
importance, and the eighth and final season
has provided plenty of them.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:16.160
Let's look at some of the tiny details you
may have missed in the last few episodes.

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:20.680
One of the first lines spoken in the first
episode of the eighth season comes from Jon

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.220
Snow, who tells Daenerys:

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.300
"Northerners don't much trust outsiders."

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:30.200
This becomes entirely clear when Jon's sister
Sansa looks skeptical if not downright contemptuous

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.760
when faced with the Dragon Queen.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.820
Daenerys doesn't exactly ingratiate herself
with the Northerners throughout the episode,

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:40.079
and they remain unwilling to trust her, despite
Jon's assurances.

00:00:40.079 --> 00:00:43.949
There's plenty of foreshadowing here about
how Daenerys and Jon will fare in the North

00:00:43.949 --> 00:00:47.949
once people learn more about their chosen
king: Not only was Jon Snow actually born

00:00:47.949 --> 00:00:52.260
in Dorne, but he's a highborn and Southern
heir to the Iron Throne.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:56.539
This makes him an outsider, even though he
seems like a Northerner through and through.

00:00:56.539 --> 00:00:58.670
Daenerys was always going to face opposition.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:02.440
But when Jon's people learn the truth about
his parentage, they might turn on the King

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:02.940
in the North.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.100
It wouldn't be the first time, either.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.020
In Game of Thrones' seventh season, it seemed
like Cersei Lannister had something to live

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:09.520
for.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:14.460
After losing her three children to poisonings
and suicide, she says she's pregnant again,

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.640
and it's a baby she conceived with her twin
brother Jaime.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:22.640
During that moment, it seems like Cersei might
start to care about something other than herself.

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:27.760
It's an oddly comforting development, particularly
for fans who were worried that Cersei might

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.820
turn into a full-fledged psychopath.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:34.040
Cersei memorably refused a glass of wine back
in season 7.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:38.420
But in the season eight premiere, she's seen
comfortably sipping wine after her first night

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:40.140
with Euron Greyjoy.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:42.159
At one point, Greyjoy tells her:

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:43.700
"I'm going to put a prince in your belly."

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:47.960
She appears to be on the verge of tears as
he walks away.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.820
Perhaps something tragic happened to the baby
since the end of season seven.

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:56.060
But knowing Cersei, it's certainly possible
that she made up the pregnancy in the first

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:59.020
place, all in an attempt to get her brothers
to side with her.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:04.180
Either way, that glass of wine seems significant,
especially considering the way she usually

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:04.680
hits the bottle.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:09.819
When Qyburn interrupts Bronn at the brothel
on behalf of the queen, viewers know the reason

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:10.840
must be an evil one.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:15.640
Ever since Cersei's brothers Jaime and Tyrion
turned on her, she's been out for revenge.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.580
And she and Qyburn seem to think Bronn is
the man to inflict that revenge.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.280
Well, audiences might want to take a second
look at his weapon.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:28.080
If the crossbow looks familiar, it's because
it's the exact same weapon Tyrion used to

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:31.980
kill his father Tywin at the end of the show's
fourth season.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.080
"Tyrion, put down the crossbow."

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:40.140
In regards to Cersei, Qyburn even tells Bron
that:

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:42.880
"She has a keen sense of poetic justice."

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.040
That's quite the understatement.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:51.040
It remains to be seen whether Bronn will ultimately
turn on both his former allies for his own

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:51.580
benefit.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:56.140
At the end of the season's first episode,
Jon Snow finally learns that he's the child

00:02:56.140 --> 00:03:01.060
of Lyanna Stark and Rhaegar Targaryen, which
makes him the true heir to the Iron Throne.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:05.820
That's information we, as viewers, have known
for a while, but Jon's been in the dark this

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:06.500
whole time.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:10.680
Still, there are plenty of clues about the
impending reveal leading up that scene.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:14.960
Throughout the episode, there are several
offhand comments about who Jon really "is"

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:15.920
or who he has "become."

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:19.040
Remember the comments made by young Lyanna
Mormont?

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:23.260
The Lady Lyanna - who's named after Jon Snow's
real mother - tells him:

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.900
"You left the North a king and came back a…

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.200
I'm not sure what you are now."

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.820
But the biggest moment hinting at Jon's big
reveal is his ride atop a dragon.

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:40.560
After all, only Targaryens can ride dragons,
and Jon rides an especially significant one.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:45.340
While Daenerys takes her place atop Drogon,
Jon mounts Rhaegal, named for his real father.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:49.900
Also worth noting: when Sam tells Jon about
his real heritage, the two are standing right

00:03:49.901 --> 00:03:53.190
in front of Ned Stark's statue in Winterfell's
crypts.

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:54.880
Remember the last time Jon saw Ned?

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.280
He made a promise:

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:00.320
"The next time we see each other, we'll talk
about your mother."

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:06.100
That makes it particularly fitting that Jon
learns the big news with a statue of his adoptive

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:06.960
father at his side.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:10.880
Jaime Lannister's return to Winterfell was
bound to be a rough one.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:15.420
After all, the last time he was there, he
tried murdering a young Bran Stark after the

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:20.060
boy caught him and his twin sister Cersei
doing things that twins really aren't supposed

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:20.580
to do.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.400
As if that weren't bad enough, though, he's
guilty of murdering Daenerys' father, which

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.000
earned him the name "Kingslayer."

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:32.320
Suffice to say, he doesn't receive a particularly
warm welcome, even after his friend Brienne

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:34.060
of Tarth vouches for his character.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:38.580
Though he's granted a royal reprieve by the
Mother of Dragons, it soon becomes clear that

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:40.890
he doesn't have a lot of faith in his new
queen.

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:42.620
"And she is… different?"

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:44.220
"She is."

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:45.480
"You're sure about her?"

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:46.420
"I am."

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:50.400
Keep in mind that Daenerys' father had a nickname
of his own: "The Mad King."

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.200
For obvious reasons, Jaime has never had anything
good to say about him:

00:04:54.700 --> 00:05:00.580
"He loved to watch people burn, the way their
skin blackened and blistered, and melted off

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:01.580
their bones."

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:05.060
No wonder he's distrustful of Daenerys.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:07.400
Especially considering her own fondness for
fire.

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:21.840
If Daenerys is poised to turn into the Mad
Queen, as many fans suspect, Jaime will have

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.060
been right not to trust her.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:26.010
Only time will tell how all that plays out.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:27.940
Until then, we'll be watching closely.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:28.800
So closely...

